<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/crusades"><span class="enc-name">Crusades</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Crusades were a series of religious wars launched by Latin Christians from the late eleventh century, chiefly to capture and hold Jerusalem and the Holy Land.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/the-crystal-palace"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/the-crystal-palace.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">The Crystal Palace</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Crystal Palace was a building of cast iron and glass designed by Joseph Paxton to house the Great Exhibition in Hyde Park, London, in 1851.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/csanad-commander"><span class="enc-name">Csanád (commander)</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Csanád was a Hungarian commander of the early 11th century in the service of King Stephen I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ctesias"><span class="enc-name">Ctesias</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ctesias of Cnidus was a Greek physician and historian of the late 5th and early 4th centuries BCE who served at the Persian court of Artaxerxes II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ctesiphon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/ctesiphon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ctesiphon</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ctesiphon was a city on the Tigris River in central Iraq, near present-day Baghdad.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/cu-chonnacht-maguire"><span class="enc-name">Cú Chonnacht Maguire</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Cú Chonnacht Maguire was lord of Fermanagh, succeeding his brother Hugh Maguire after Hugh's death in 1600 during the Nine Years' War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cu-chulainn"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cu-chulainn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cú Chulainn</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Cú Chulainn is the greatest hero of the Ulster Cycle of Irish legend, a nephew of King Conchobar mac Nessa.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cuacuauhpitzahuac"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cuacuauhpitzahuac.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cuacuauhpitzahuac</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Cuacuauhpitzahuac was the first tlatoani of Tlatelolco, the twin city of Tenochtitlan in the Valley of Mexico, ruling from the 1370s to about 1418.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cuauhtemoc"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cuauhtemoc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cuauhtémoc</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Cuauhtémoc was the last ruler of Tenochtitlan and of the Aztec Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cuba"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cuba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cuba</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Cuba is the largest island of the Caribbean, colonised by Spain from the early sixteenth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cuban-missile-crisis"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cuban-missile-crisis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cuban Missile Crisis</span><span class="enc-type">Crisis · 1962</span><span class="enc-snip">The Cuban Missile Crisis of October 1962 was the closest the Cold War came to nuclear war.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cuban-revolution"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cuban-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cuban Revolution</span><span class="enc-type">Revolution · 1953–1959</span><span class="enc-snip">The Cuban Revolution was the armed rising led by Fidel Castro and his 26th of July Movement against the dictatorship of Fulgencio Batista.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cuban-revolutionary-party"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cuban-revolutionary-party.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cuban Revolutionary Party</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Cuban Revolutionary Party was founded in 1892 by José Martí among Cuban and Puerto Rican exiles in the United States to prepare and finance a war for the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cudjoe"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cudjoe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cudjoe</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Cudjoe was the leader of the Leeward Maroons of western Jamaica, communities of escaped enslaved Africans in the Cockpit Country.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cuenca-ecuador"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cuenca-ecuador.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cuenca, Ecuador</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Cuenca is the third-largest city of Ecuador and capital of Azuay province, in the southern highlands.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cuenca-spain"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cuenca-spain.jpg" alt=""