"/encyclopedia/cybele"><span class="enc-name">Cybele</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Cybele was the mother goddess of Anatolia, worshipped by the Phrygians as Matar, 'Mother', often shown in rock-cut shrines in the highlands.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cyclades"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cyclades.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cyclades</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Cyclades are a group of about 220 islands in the southern Aegean Sea, so called because they form a rough circle around the sacred island of Delos.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cyclone-nargis"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cyclone-nargis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cyclone Nargis</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">Cyclone Nargis was a tropical cyclone that struck Myanmar on 2–3 May 2008, driving a storm surge across the Irrawaddy delta.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cyfraith-hywel"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cyfraith-hywel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cyfraith Hywel</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Cyfraith Hywel, the law of Hywel, was the native law of medieval Wales, traditionally said to have been codified under Hywel Dda in the 10th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/cyirima-ii-rujugira"><span class="enc-name">Cyirima II Rujugira</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Cyirima II Rujugira was a king (mwami) of Rwanda in the eighteenth century, whose exact dates are uncertain.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/cylon-of-athens"><span class="enc-name">Cylon of Athens</span><span cla