/czech-republic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Czech Republic</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Czech Republic, or Czechia, is a landlocked country in central Europe made up of the historical lands of Bohemia, Moravia and Czech Silesia, with Prague as its…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/czech-silesia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/czech-silesia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Czech Silesia</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Czech Silesia is the part of the historical region of Silesia that lies in the Czech Republic, around Opava and Ostrava.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovak-legion"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/czechoslovak-legion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Czechoslovak Legion</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Czechoslovak Legion was a force of Czech and Slovak volunteers, many of them former prisoners of war, who fought for the Allies in the First World War, above all in…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovak-national-council"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/czechoslovak-national-council.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Czechoslovak National Council</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Czechoslovak National Council was the organisation of the Czech and Slovak independence movement abroad, founded in Paris in 1916 with Tomáš Garrigue Masaryk as…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovak-new-wave"><span class="enc-name">Czechoslovak New Wave</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">The Czechoslovak New Wave was a movement